Is it possible for Str_copy or Str_concat to call assert to verify
that the destination memory area specified by the caller is large
enough? Explain.

This is not going to be possible because the assert call is able to 
simply check if the pointer is somewhere null or not, but it is not able
to directly access it or see how much space in memory it takes up. So, 
it does not have this capability and checking if it is big enough in 
memory will have to be done some other way.

